{
  "id": "021",
  "title": "My Grandmother's Wedding",
  "subtitle": "\"My 78-year-old grandmother was getting married for the third time. She demanded I bring a 'serious boyfriend.' I asked the coffee-shop regular I'd been mildly in love with since spring.\"",
  "penName": "Sunny Ogden",
  "genre": "fakeDating",
  "hook": "My grandmother Millicent was seventy-eight. She had buried two husbands. She was about to marry her third in six weeks. She called me at the bookstore where I work — the Back Pages, in Brattleboro — and informed me that if I showed up to her Vermont wedding alone, she would personally introduce me to her fiancé's seventy-five-year-old widowed nephew as \"available.\" I asked Theodore Ash, the coffee-shop regular I had been mildly in love with since March, if he would drive to my grandmother's wedding with me and pretend, for one weekend, to be serious. He closed his book and said yes.",
